<BaseLayout title="Mission & end state" description="UXO.INFO works toward a world free from the threat of UXO and explosive remnants of war, through honest, source-led public information.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Mission / end state</p><h1>Our goal is a world free from the threat.</h1><p class="lead">UXO.INFO exists because unexploded ordnance and other explosive remnants of war still put people, communities, land, and water at risk. The long-term aim is for this site to become unnecessary.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">What we mean</p><h2>Clear the threat. Keep the truth.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>We support the objective of finding, clearing, removing, or safely destroying known explosive hazards through trained professionals, accountable institutions, and established standards. We also support the records, local capacity, risk education, and environmental care that make that work durable.</p><p>UXO.INFO does not promise that every item can be located or that an area can be known to be free of every possible explosive object. Ordnance can be buried, submerged, undocumented, displaced, or discovered decades later.</p><p>Responsible mine action works from evidence. It applies professional survey, defined land-release processes, and <em>all reasonable effort</em>—not impossible promises of absolute certainty.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--deep"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Residual reality</p><h2>Completion and certainty are not the same thing.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>International Mine Action Standards recognize residual contamination and residual risk: hazards or risk that may remain after all reasonable effort has been applied. A later discovery needs a serious response, but it is not automatically proof that a responsibly documented clearance process failed.</p><p>The practical end state is not pretending that uncertainty has disappeared. It is a world where explosive remnants no longer shape daily life, and where sustainable national systems can respond safely to the exceptional discovery that still occurs.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">The archive we hope for</p><h2>One day, this should be historical record.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Until the threat is gone, UXO.INFO should help people understand the issue, locate reliable sources, and leave hazardous objects to trained professionals. It is not a clearance organization or an emergency service.</p><p>Our best possible future is for UXO.INFO to remain online only as an archive: evidence of a problem people once had to warn one another about.</p><a class="action-link" href="/resources">Read the standards and source library</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
